sons_made":1,"stopping_rule":"Fixed horizon: the holdout is read once, at its end. No interim look decides the test."},"machine":{"window_dates":{"training":["2026-09-09","2026-10-27"],"validation":["2026-10-27","2027-02-16"],"holdout":["2027-09-01","2029-02-20"]},"window_note":"[from, to): dates of the games inside each window, Eastern","minimum_sample":80,"alpha_one_sided":0.0125,"version":"1.0.0-prereg","status":"EXPERIMENTAL","provenance":"T3"}},{"id":"H-NFL-STALE-01","title":"Stale contest lines","hypothesis":"Sides flagged by the snapshot delta detector capture positive CLV from snapshot to close above baseline.","objective":"Measure whether a material move after the Thursday freeze, seen BEFORE the close, leaves the frozen number on the side the market moved toward with value at the close more often than smaller moves do — the stale-contest-line effect.","unit":"One NFL game with a Thursday freeze (status ok) and a close (status ok).","decision_time":"Saturday 12:00 ET of the contest week (the current number is read then from capture history with nfl_consensus_spread_at). The flag computed AT THE CLOSE is hindsight and is never the treatment.","treatment":"Games flagged at decision time: |current − freeze| ≥ 1.0 or the move touched 3, 6, 7, 10 or 14. Side = the side the market had moved toward at decision time.","baseline":"Games not flagged at decision time whose number had moved (nonzero delta). Side = the side it had moved toward.","outcome":"CLV of the frozen best price on that side at the frozen number at the close (as H-NFL-KEY-01). Positive CLV = success.","primary_metric":"Treatment rate of CLV > 0 minus baseline rate of CLV > 0 (two-proportion z, one-sided).","secondary_metrics":["mean CLV difference with a bootstrap 95% interval","the share of flagged moves that reversed by the close"],"training_window":"None fitted. 2026 Weeks 1–7 reconstructed freezes: pipeline check only, not evidence.","validation_window":"2026 Week 8 through the 2026 postseason