he holdout."},"machine":{"window_dates":{"training":null,"validation":["2026-10-27","2027-01-12"],"holdout":["2027-09-01","2028-01-12"]},"window_note":"[from, to): dates of the games inside each window, Eastern","minimum_sample":60,"alpha_one_sided":0.0125,"version":"1.0.0-prereg","status":"EXPERIMENTAL","provenance":"T3"}},{"id":"H-NFL-DIV-01","title":"Divisional underdogs","hypothesis":"Divisional underdogs cover above 50% after controlling for the line.","objective":"Measure whether underdogs in division games cover the closing number more often than non-divisional underdogs at the same number.","unit":"One NFL regular-season game with a nonzero closing line (football/pricing/lines_nfl.json, nflverse consensus close); side = the closing underdog. Divisional = nflverse div_game (era-correct; the seeded nfl_team_divisions table agrees for 2026).","treatment":"Divisional games.","baseline":"Non-divisional games, matched on closing-line stratum: 0.5–2.5, 3, 3.5–6.5, 7, 7.5–9.5, 10–13.5, 14+.","outcome":"The underdog covers the closing line. Pushes excluded.","primary_metric":"Mantel–Haenszel risk difference (divisional minus non-divisional underdog cover rate) across the line strata, one-sided; and the stratum-standardised divisional underdog cover rate against 0.50.","secondary_metrics":["home and road divisional underdogs separately","logistic regression cover ~ divisional + line stratum + season"],"training_window":"2002–2019 regular seasons (the current alignment). Exploratory: the estimate and its interval are reported; nothing is tuned.","validation_window":"2020–2025 regular seasons: the direction must agree with training for the study to proceed to the holdout read.","holdout_window":"2026 Week 8 through 2027 Week 18 (prospective; 2026 Weeks 1–7 are excluded because the season-to-date divisional records are displayed on the card).","minimum_sample":{"divisional_underdogs_validation":400,"divisional_underdogs_holdout":120},"decision_rule":"passed = true only if the validation risk difference is positive AND, on the holdout, the risk difference is positive with one-sided p < 0.0125 AND the standardised divisional underdog cover rate exceeds 0.50 AND the minimum samples are met.","forking_paths":{"alternatives_considered":["the opener instead of the close","home divisional underdogs only","regression adjustment as primary","including the postseason"],"choice_and_reason":"The close is the line EdgeDesk owns for every season; all divisional underdogs (home and road) is the stated hypothesis; MH stratification is the simplest control for the line; postseason division games are rare and excluded.","data_already_seen":"Before registration, the 2026 season-to-date records through Week 6 were computed and displayed on the card: divisional underdogs 20-8 (28 graded), divisional home underdogs 7-4 (11). Those weeks are outside every window of this study (the holdout starts 2026-10-27). No divisional ATS rate was computed for 2002-2025. EdgeDesk's NFL engine carries a divisional feature fitted on historical seasons, so the training and validation seasons are not naive to the divisional effect on margins; the prospective holdout is.","comparisons_made":1,"stopping_rule":"Training and validation are read once at registration's first analysis; the holdout once at the end of 2027 Week 18."},"machine":{"window_dates":{"training":["2002-09-01","2020-03-01"],"validation":["2020-09-01","2026-03-01"],"holdout":["2026-10-27","2028-01-12"]},"window_note":"[from, to): dates of the games inside each window, Eastern","minimum_sample":120,"alpha_one_sided":0.0125,"version":"1.0.0-prereg","status":"EXPERIMENTAL","provenance":"T3"}}]}$prereg$::jsonb;
